Apologia de Sócrates / Críton — Carlos Alberto Nunes (@greek-source-plato-pt: 0, is #book, #part-of @greek-portuguese-editions) { r_5653D0KAK9093C4VMSTEZJ3MBW
Platão. Tradução de Carlos Alberto Nunes; texto grego de John Burnet; coordenação de Benedito Nunes e Victor Sales Pinheiro. Apologia de Sócrates / Críton, 4ª edição, bilíngue. Belém: EdUFPA, 2023. ISBN 9786589745051. Portuguese and Ancient Greek.

[Publisher and edition](https://vendasonline.editora.ufpa.br/filosofia/apologia-de-socrates-criton-ed--4-95/p).

**Read with:** [Apology: why examine a life?](../socratic/Apology.lingua#r_0DWAPFJNVYT6WNTRT46ZVK82X4) and [Crito: law, conscience, and a difficult decision](../socratic/Crito.lingua#r_54N10WGKCSCKW6XM202PCG7ZDH). The works answer the same guide questions when read in this translation. Consult the translator's introductions after a first reading of the relevant primary passages.

For comparison, use the retained [Cary edition](Socratic-dialogues-Cary.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001005) or [Jowett volume](Dialogues-Jowett.lingua#r_1AD7N0E0ZYZ07XSMQWSK5PA5X8). The parallel Greek also supports [the optional work on reading the original language](../languages/Read-original-texts.lingua#r_1Q07KPDNG2JTY7HRWQY5H6T5MJ).

**Access:** publisher, library, or an owned copy. **Reuse:** publisher's terms.

